    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d710">

                <pb facs="0704" n="1438" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1438"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pera</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1895-12-31"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                    1895</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Missionaries at all interior posts reported safe and protected by soldiers.
                    Bloody outbreak Ourfa 28th. Safe-conduct promised for Miss Shattuck, who is
                    there alone, to Aintab. Porte agrees that relief for destitute at Harpoot may be
                    extended under a commission of three—Barnum, one Turk, one native Christian. He
                    has American and English charity funds. The Porte denies complicity of officers
                    or soldiers in destroying American property. Am ready with data as to damages to
                    demand indemnity. Shall I do so now and consent to send a commission to inquire
                    if requested, or wait for further instructions?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
